Kind: ablation
Issue: #764
Over: 764-widen-console-gap.patch
Takes out: what #764 changed in libposix-uros's __uros_writev() -- a terminal's pieces go back to being written one by one, through __uros_write(), as before #764.  hello_server's stdout stays line-buffered, so its line arm goes over as writev() of what the buffer holds and " (#764)\n": two console writes, the first leaving the line open, and the widen's line lands in the gap.  scripts/suite-i386.sh never finds the arm's line whole.
Run: i386 -- UROS_BUILD_DIR=<worktree>/uros/build scripts/suite-i386.sh -r bundle-kvm-4, from a worktree with 764-widen-console-gap.patch and this one, and a build of its own; scripts/ablate.sh cannot judge it
Expect: never said: \(hello_server\): console: a line of \[0-9\]\* characters

